[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. The reports in it
show three problems. Each problem needs its own fix, so each problem now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the parser reports. The other two problems stay open after it ships.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts as the [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) does, from the same export. Each report
counts once, by its id, under its cause. The `shift` reports stay under the cause their tenant
files them in, and they also get their own ticket. The counts change when the desk merges more reports.

## How a report is placed

1. **`shift`**: the desk read the report as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`, `oneDayMove`).
   The day of the month is kept, but the invite lands one day early. The bodies say
   "Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May" and "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
   Toronto got Monday". A month/day flip cannot make this. Look for a time zone conversion.
2. **`hint`**: a day-first tenant on `booking-v3`, through the form. The form prints
   `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so people type the month first, and the form then reads
   the date day first. The parser fix does not touch this.
3. **`parser`**: any other report from a day-first tenant. The shared parser reads every date
   month first, so 7 April becomes 4 July.

The tenant decides the cause, not the intake tag. Intake guesses `hint` from an `en-US` browser,
and that guess is wrong in both directions: the [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) shows the tags
under each cause.

## Why one ticket hid three

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. All three
  problems produce the same subjects: "Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong".
- The <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="shift" /> one-day reports were noted in a footnote under
  `parser`. A footnote is not a ticket.
- The <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> `hint` reports were marked "not this
  ticket", but nobody opened a ticket for them.

## What to do

- Track each fix on its own ticket (links in the table). Close #4471 only when all three close.
- Merge a new date report by its tenant, form and channel, with the rules above. Not by subject.

